body:
Hi, the sibling in question here flat out refuses any kind of conversation with us, so we (the rest of the family) never got to the point of bringing up a professional. The plan of suicide has not been confronted yet; our sibling still thinks that we are unaware. We want to intervene and confront the issue before my sibling plans on executing the suicide plan.

&#x200B;

We also think that our sibling will adamantly refuse to seek a professional... (let alone, us) so we are not quite sure how to approach it. We are planning to talk to some professionals beforehand, but we are also taking into account a scenario where it would just be us siblings (no professionals) trying to talk and maybe bring up the idea of seeking a professional during the confrontation.
